{
	title: 'Subagents report back by themselves; spawn starts fresh',
	spec: "A subagent's answer reaches its parent without the send tool: when a turn of a subagent-kind session that its parent started (the first task, or a later message from the parent) ends, the host delivers the turn's last assistant text to the parent as a message from the child, advisory like any agent message. A turn that ends with no assistant text still reports: 'Session <label> finished without a message'; one that ends failed or paused says so and why ('Session <label> stopped: <reason>'), so a parent never waits for a child that has stopped. The child's first prompt no longer tells it to send a handoff; it says its last message is returned to the parent. Turns the user starts in a promoted (left-open) subagent report nothing. spawn's mode defaults to fresh for every kind (questions: user's answers of 27 Sep): a subagent gets clear guidance in its task instead of the parent's context; fork stays available on request. Messages from other sessions to a session the user paused wait until he continues it (as task rj built).",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"User decision (27 Sep): when the user steers into a turn the parent started, he takes the wheel: the subagent is promoted (no auto-close, as in the old Hal), but that turn's last message still goes to the parent, which is probably waiting for it.",
		"subagents.report(id) runs after every turn end: in runTurn after the status transition (before prompts.next and finished, so the label still names the tab) and in turns.stop's on-disk pause. It sends with prompts.submit(parent, text, …, { from: child, label, advisory: true }), after host.ready(parent).",
		"Who owes a report (subagents.owed) is read from history, not kept in memory: a turn-starting user record whose first text is from the parent makes the work the parent's; one from the human (no from) makes it the user's; a `continue` keeps the paused turn's owner; a turn started by the child's own subagent (meta.parent === child) inherits, so a child that waited reports when its subagents' results come in. Turns started by other sessions report nothing.",
		"Decision: a turn that ended at wait (completed, reason tool_use) reports nothing; its work is not done. Only turn_end reason tool_use comes from wait's endTurn.",
		'A human message sent (steering) while a parent-started turn runs joins that turn, so its answer still reports to the parent; only a turn the human starts is silent.',
		'The report is the last non-blank assistant text block of the final turn only (records after the previous turn_end), not texts of earlier rounds.',
		'Fixture: pausing a session in host tests needs the client to open it first.',
		'Reports from an owned child do not wake a parent whose tab was closed (task 8v), even if the parent was idle when closed; non-tab sessions still receive reports.'
